maria: Hey team — quick poll: what's our recommended approach for `fetch` in the JS SDK across ESM/CJS + edge vs node? runtime detect, bundle-time polyfill, or require users to pass a fetch impl?

jon: runtime detect + allow injection. keeps SDK small and works for most cases. detect with `globalThis.fetch` and fall back to lazy import of `undici` in node.

sam (devex): Agree. Suggest default behavior: 1) use global fetch if available 2) try `await import('undici')` and use `undici.fetch` 3) if neither, error with clear message and example to pass `fetch` in client options.

kyle: One gotcha: some bundlers polyfill fetch incorrectly (no streaming). Edge runtimes (Cloudflare/Vercel Edge) have proper fetch, so fallback should only run in Node. Also watch ESM/CJS entrypoints — dynamic import works in both if we ship ESM.

maria: Can someone paste a tiny code snippet we can put in README? short and copy/paste friendly.

jon: Sure — something like:

```js
// tiny helper inside sdk
export async function getFetch() {
  if (typeof globalThis.fetch === 'function') return globalThis.fetch;
  try {
    const { fetch } = await import('undici');
    return fetch;
  } catch (e) {
    throw new Error('No fetch available. Pass a fetch implementation to the client: new RedwoodClient({ fetch: yourFetch })');
  }
}
```

sam (devex): For types, recommend the client option be typed as `fetch?: typeof globalThis.fetch` so TS users get correct signatures. Also mention `lib.dom` in tsconfig for Node consumers who don't have DOM libs.

kyle: Also add helper snippet for tests that need a deterministic polyfill, e.g. `globalThis.fetch = (await import('undici')).fetch` in jest setup.

maria: Good points. What about packaging advice? conditional exports?

jon: Use conditional exports in package.json: "\"exports\": { \".\": { \"import\": \"./dist/index.mjs\", \"require\": \"./dist/index.cjs\" } }" and ship ESM-first build. Keeps dynamic import sane.

sam (devex): And add an examples folder: `examples/node` and `examples/edge` that show the minimal setup + how to pass custom fetch. Onboarding friction drops a lot with tiny copy/paste samples.

maria: I'll open a PR for README + examples + a small helper util based on Jon's snippet. tagging @kyle to add a test-case matrix for Node 16/18/20 + edge runtimes. :thumbsup:

ci-bot: Created issue #3421: "SDK: fetch polyfill guidance + examples" — link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/issues/3421

maria: thanks — let's keep the fallback lazy and explicit errors so customers aren't surprised.

jon: Also add a short troubleshooting blurb: "If you see `fetch is not defined`, either run Node >=18, add `undici` as a dependency, or pass `fetch` to the client."

sam (devex): I'll draft the TS types PR and include `fetch?: typeof globalThis.fetch` in constructor options, plus a note about `--lib DOM` for TS consumers.

maria: perfect, thanks everyone. closing loop once PRs are up.
